            "text_Pnm68r": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "t:names.text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<h1>SKRE Product Warranty</h1><h3>Built for the Hunt. Backed by SKRE.</h3><p>At SKRE, we stand behind the quality, craftsmanship, and performance of our gear. Our products are built for demanding hunting conditions, and we are committed to delivering gear our customers can depend on.</p><p>We offer a <strong>Limited Lifetime Warranty against manufacturing defects in materials and workmanship</strong> for the reasonable functional lifespan of the product.</p><p>Our warranty protects against manufacturing defects, not normal wear and tear, misuse, or deterioration from extended use.</p><h3>Warranty Eligibility</h3><ul><li>Applies to products used for personal, non-commercial purposes.</li><li>Covers manufacturing defects within the product's reasonable functional lifespan.</li><li>Product lifetime refers to the <strong>usable life of the gear, not the lifetime of the owner.</strong></li><li>Lifespan depends on usage, conditions, care, and overall product condition.</li><li>Proof of purchase may be required.</li></ul><h3>What Our Warranty Covers</h3><p>Verified manufacturing defects, including:</p><ul><li><strong>Materials:</strong> Premature fabric or material failure due to manufacturing defects.</li><li><strong>Zippers:</strong> Defective zipper materials, construction, or installation.</li><li><strong>Buttons, buckles, and closures:</strong> Failures caused by faulty materials or workmanship.</li><li><strong>Seams and stitching:</strong> Premature separation caused by manufacturing defects.</li><li><strong>Coatings and lamination:</strong> Premature peeling or delamination resulting from manufacturing defects.</li><li><strong>Craftsmanship:</strong> Other verified manufacturing or assembly defects.</li></ul><p><strong>Important:</strong> Component failure alone does not establish a manufacturing defect. Product age, condition, and usage are considered when evaluating claims.</p><h3>What Our Warranty Does Not Cover</h3><ul><li>Normal wear and tear or products beyond their reasonable functional lifespan.</li><li>Zippers worn or damaged through extended use, excessive force, debris, or improper maintenance.</li><li>Abrasion, punctures, tears, cuts, burns, or damage from conditions beyond intended use.</li><li>Improper washing, drying, storage, or care.</li><li>Misuse, accidents, alterations, or unauthorized repairs.</li><li>Cosmetic deterioration or gradual performance loss from aging and use.</li><li>Branded lifestyle apparel, including t-shirts and hoodies.</li><li>Socks, underwear, and boxers.</li></ul><h3>Warranty Claim Assessment</h3><p>All claims are reviewed by SKRE, considering:</p><ul><li>Product age and overall condition.</li><li>Extent of wear and evidence of use.</li><li>Nature and location of the failure.</li><li>Whether the issue reflects a manufacturing defect or normal deterioration.</li><li>Maintenance history, where relevant.</li></ul><p><strong>A failed component on a heavily worn garment does not automatically qualify for warranty coverage, even if that component is normally covered.</strong></p><p>SKRE reserves the right to determine eligibility following a reasonable assessment.</p><h3>Warranty Resolution</h3><p>For approved claims, SKRE may:</p><ul><li>Repair the defective product.</li><li>Replace it with the same or a comparable product.</li><li>Offer an alternative resolution when repair or replacement is impractical.</li></ul><p>Replacement is not guaranteed when a reasonable repair can restore functionality.</p><h3>Our Commitment</h3><p>We understand that hunters depend on their gear in demanding environments. Our commitment is to stand behind genuine manufacturing defects while maintaining a fair and sustainable warranty program.</p><p><strong>We stand behind our craftsmanship. We do not guarantee against the natural effects of time, use, and wear.</strong></p>",
                "width": "100%",
